WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:02.658
The Spark job ran for six hours.

2
00:00:02.678 --> 00:00:04.555
Yesterday it took one.

3
00:00:04.575 --> 00:00:07.042
A senior engineer can say why it is slow.

4
00:00:07.062 --> 00:00:08.890
Not only how to write it.

5
00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:14.040
Three things explain most slow jobs: shuffles, skew, and small files.

6
00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.500
First: how does Spark run your code?

7
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.175
The driver makes the plan.

8
00:00:18.195 --> 00:00:21.510
The executors do the work, in many small tasks.

9
00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:23.910
A transformation only adds to the plan.

10
00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:25.720
Nothing runs yet.

11
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.320
The work starts at an action.

12
00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.270
For example, a write or a count.

13
00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.005
Second: the shuffle.

14
00:00:32.025 --> 00:00:35.168
A join or a group by must bring the same keys together.

15
00:00:35.188 --> 00:00:37.640
So data moves between machines.

16
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.165
That move is the shuffle.

17
00:00:39.185 --> 00:00:42.025
It is the most costly step in most jobs.

18
00:00:42.045 --> 00:00:44.525
If one table is small, broadcast it.

19
00:00:44.545 --> 00:00:47.500
Then the big table does not shuffle.

20
00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.160
Third: one key has most of the rows.

21
00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:51.148
That is skew.

22
00:00:51.168 --> 00:00:54.720
One task gets most of the data, and runs for hours.

23
00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:56.932
In the Spark U I, you see it at once.

24
00:00:56.952 --> 00:00:59.605
One task is far slower than the rest.

25
00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:01.880
Turn on adaptive query execution.

26
00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.880
Or add a salt to split the hot key.

27
00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.340
Last: thousands of small files.

28
00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.753
Each file costs a listing and an open.

29
00:01:09.773 --> 00:01:12.725
Many small files make every reader slow.

30
00:01:12.745 --> 00:01:14.825
So write fewer, bigger files.

31
00:01:14.845 --> 00:01:17.825
And compact the table on a schedule.

32
00:01:17.845 --> 00:01:19.710
Quick recap of Spark.

33
00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:21.047
Actions start the work.

34
00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:22.560
Shuffles cost the most.

35
00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:25.245
And skew shows as one slow task.

36
00:01:25.265 --> 00:01:28.365
Now start the first lesson below.
